From d8c6b5f378c11b078622ca1ef5e0a036a3af8c77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 12:59:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): an SSH-attached Desktop Stop reads "Stopped by
 Desktop", and every Stop names its gesture [daveey]

A Desktop attached over SSH logs in with its per-connection ownership id (provider desktop-ssh), so
the stop notice read "Stopped by 5caca28140205b2b8f1f5cabb2aaf8ba". And every Stop door (Stop
button, Esc, tile, /stop, delete) sent an identical session.interrupt, so "why did this stop?" had
no answer in agent.log.

- _stop_issuer_label: a desktop-ssh identity is "Desktop"; real logins still show the login.
- session.interrupt accepts an optional free-form `origin` (contract + regenerated TS/OpenRPC).
  The gateway logs it on the session.interrupt line (origin=<x> or origin=-) and keeps it in the
  turn_stopped notice metadata as stop_origin; made log-safe, capped at 64 chars, never inherited
  by a later turn's Stop.
- Desktop sends it: stop_button, esc, tile / tile:esc, slash, delete, send_now, transcript,
  rewind, plugin:hermes-bots (lib/stop-origin.ts). The canonical protocol strips it (its control
  contract forbids unknown keys).
